WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:02.670
- [Narrator] These are
Chinese medical workers

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:05.240
arriving at Wuhan Red Cross Hospital

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:07.400
with a patient suspected of infection

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.730
with a new coronavirus.

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:12.460
The workers are wearing
personal protective equipment,

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:14.650
or PPE, designed to prevent

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:17.590
exposure to infectious materials.

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:20.060
Infections and deaths
from the novel coronavirus

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:21.990
have continued to rise throughout China

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:23.143
and around the world.

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:25.460
According to the U.S. Centers

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:27.330
for Disease Control and Prevention,

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:30.043
how the new virus spreads
isn't completely understood.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:33.520
Here's the protective equipment
that healthcare workers

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:36.380
have worn during major
outbreaks such as SARS and Ebola

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:37.850
and why it's crucial in the battle

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:40.710
against the novel coronavirus epidemic.

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:43.910
- PPE is used for a variety of hazards.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:46.960
In the healthcare world,
one of the biggest hazards

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:48.570
is microbial and that could be

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:50.850
viruses, bacteria, fungi, et cetera.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:54.200
Some are fine-air particles
that enter your lungs.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.840
Some are contact materials.

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:59.630
Others can enter through various orifices,

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:01.210
your nose or eyes.

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:03.380
So when we're choosing
PPE, it's very important

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:05.110
to understand the transmission.

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:07.070
- [Narrator] Coronavirus is likely spread

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:10.700
through a cough, sneeze or
other contact with saliva.

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:13.170
But because much is
unknown about the virus,

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:15.130
healthcare workers are
following precautions

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:17.103
to prevent different types of exposure.

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:20.510
- So today when you look at
personal protective equipment

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:23.460
for microbial risk, such as coronavirus,

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:25.680
you're looking at four
items and they would be

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:29.580
a face shield followed by
a respirator of some sort

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:34.580
followed by a disposable
coverall and finally gloves.

00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:38.650
- [Narrator] Coveralls, face
shields, goggles and gloves

00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:40.640
protect against hazards like Ebola,

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:43.950
that can spread by direct
contact with bodily fluids.

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:46.130
The respirator prevents
inhering droplets in the air

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:47.790
from sneezes and coughs.

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:49.460
Healthcare workers wore respirators

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:52.633
while treating patients during
the SARS and MERS outbreaks.

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:57.410
- The most sort of effective
way of these pathogens

00:01:57.410 --> 00:02:00.500
entering your body is through
the respiratory system.

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:03.550
So that's why most PPE
in healthcare settings

00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:06.140
tends to focus around
respiratory protection,

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:08.930
protecting what comes into your lungs.

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:11.060
- [Narrator] The
highly-infectious nature of Ebola

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:13.450
led to the death of
healthcare workers in Africa

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:16.800
and exposed a potential
fatal flaw in the use of PPE.

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.010
- We learned very
quickly that the sequence

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:21.860
of taking off the clothing
was very critical.

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:25.030
We had people making the mistake
of taking off their gloves

00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:27.350
and then taking off their respirator

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:29.870
or their eyeglasses or their face shield.

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:33.690
And that simple mistake of
taking one off before the other

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:35.860
contaminated them and, of course,

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:38.200
they ended up with the disease.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.880
- [Narrator] The Ebola epidemic prompted

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:42.267
an update of PPE guidelines by the WHO.

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:46.900
A global shortage of masks
has emerged as everyday people

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.993
try to protect themselves from the virus.

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:51.970
- As you travel the streets of any city,

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:54.610
especially in these days,
you'll see a variety

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:56.830
of respiratory protection.

00:02:56.830 --> 00:02:58.970
You'll see people wearing bandanas.

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:01.120
You'll see people wearing surgical masks.

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:04.430
You'll see people wearing
a very colorful masks

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:06.690
that they buy downtown.

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:08.820
- [Narrator] While both
respirators and surgical masks

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:11.030
are effective at filtering
out large droplets,

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:12.600
surgical masks are less effective

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:14.170
at filtering out smaller droplets,

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:16.630
which can be inhaled through
the sides of the mask.

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:19.410
- So what we have here
is an N95 respirator.

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:24.110
It's 95% efficient at
particles down to .3 microns

00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:26.100
in diameter, very, very small.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.210
As reference, your hair is 50 microns

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:31.390
so this is .3, it's a
fraction of your hair.

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:32.610
- [Narrator] As healthcare officials look

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:34.610
to contain the spread of the coronavirus,

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:36.380
they will rely on the availability

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:39.620
and proper use of PPE in impacted areas.

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:42.210
- The key to stopping this epidemic

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:45.590
is a combination of isolating
those that are infected

00:03:45.590 --> 00:03:48.360
and making sure no one gets reinfected.

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:50.300
And the key for that infection

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:52.330
would be personal protective equipment.

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:55.280
So it's not just about
you wearing the equipment

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:57.760
to protect your health, it's also about

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:00.380
stopping the disease and in this case,

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:02.300
personal protective equipment is really

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:07.000
the vital answer to stopping
this epidemic from spreading.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:10.167
(bright quirky music)

